[{:db/id "q-49762/selection/fde89b28ccecc9db465a73a81d307d94b35a8c302ffd79373ae93022d667b6e9" :answer/id #uuid "0d8fad18-3443-50e5-b9cd-1d7f93b1ee84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762/selection/0781888fd5d22ae2847c5c8ae1fba1203e0c98385e639f0f701e302c7faac595" :answer/id #uuid "d29dfc73-399e-5999-a9d3-a2a5861985b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" :answer/id #uuid "872a3d2b-76e5-5180-99df-ec8ed66227db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762/selection/31e79cfcd024a7c3551fa83d47473b4e4f9882ee1a55d89b509b2dee00fc9c6b" :answer/id #uuid "ea7a8659-cf41-5228-b5ca-730243762040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762/selection/7207d9bae4d2b85141016ffbdb2c1a7fae4c6b315d6731a9e9a3cf641ef1d7ba" :answer/id #uuid "9fdd6bd5-ca2a-50da-b915-bc4e9da9b248" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "12b4b964-78de-5a62-aba8-77a905490a9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49762/selection/fde89b28ccecc9db465a73a81d307d94b35a8c302ffd79373ae93022d667b6e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-49762/selection/fde89b28ccecc9db465a73a81d307d94b35a8c302ffd79373ae93022d667b6e9" "q-49762/selection/0781888fd5d22ae2847c5c8ae1fba1203e0c98385e639f0f701e302c7faac595" "q-49762/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" "q-49762/selection/31e79cfcd024a7c3551fa83d47473b4e4f9882ee1a55d89b509b2dee00fc9c6b" "q-49762/selection/7207d9bae4d2b85141016ffbdb2c1a7fae4c6b315d6731a9e9a3cf641ef1d7ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49762" :question/id #uuid "17651bab-0045-573e-9f10-81a57a8387d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49762" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4=(x-2)(x+2).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{2x+6}{(x-2)(x+2)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+6=A(x-2)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+6 & =A(2-2)+B(2+2) \\\\ 10 & =4B \\\\ B & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)+6 & =A(-2-2)+B(-2+2) \\\\ 2 & =-4A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}=-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-\\frac{1}{3}|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-{3}^{5}|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-1})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection/b46a89106abfbaaddd7e7797028c9f978d583e364a9adc93b2bb761d1ed0e4b9" :answer/id #uuid "661d4cdf-9f36-585a-be75-bee3668d8561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection/295dac5fa4d5d64455f39d27ce39681f8b19b2c4632faab1abe33e3d767025f0" :answer/id #uuid "bcffeced-0ae9-5682-bba0-18502342e5c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4" :answer/id #uuid "f8e48a85-4ecb-5e56-9e25-99aecb4b14e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection/a7b50e91c4359e8af2412ddd4451ddf4728e6291cb21cd54b2a36f8d20bcfc13" :answer/id #uuid "45604210-a133-5820-8d1a-34550304d1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection/7207d9bae4d2b85141016ffbdb2c1a7fae4c6b315d6731a9e9a3cf641ef1d7ba" :answer/id #uuid "6e0f473f-9419-5b16-8a6a-55e759a41868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34a3d631-8d65-5484-b5f8-21ddd0f0659b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49765/selection/b46a89106abfbaaddd7e7797028c9f978d583e364a9adc93b2bb761d1ed0e4b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-49765/selection/b46a89106abfbaaddd7e7797028c9f978d583e364a9adc93b2bb761d1ed0e4b9" "q-49765/selection/295dac5fa4d5d64455f39d27ce39681f8b19b2c4632faab1abe33e3d767025f0" "q-49765/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4" "q-49765/selection/a7b50e91c4359e8af2412ddd4451ddf4728e6291cb21cd54b2a36f8d20bcfc13" "q-49765/selection/7207d9bae4d2b85141016ffbdb2c1a7fae4c6b315d6731a9e9a3cf641ef1d7ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49765" :question/id #uuid "8143903c-337b-5c23-a61d-b90946f18ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-49765" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-7}^{-3}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+8)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n11x+46=A(x+8)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-8,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(-8)+46 & =A(-8+8)+B(-8+2) \\\\ -42 & =-6B \\\\ B & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(-2)+46 & =A(-2+8)+B(-2+2) \\\\ 24 & =6A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}=\\frac{4}{(x+2)}+\\frac{7}{(x+8)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{x+2}+\\frac{7}{x+8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{x+8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n            \n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+8|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{4}(x+8)^{7}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-7}^{-3}\\frac{11x+46}{(x+2)(x+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{4}(x+8)^{7}|{|}_{-7}^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{7})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{4}) \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49765/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348896/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7c3d8055-eede-5c29-97fe-82f360115b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348896/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1b3a98-215a-5022-815e-c7b8f7564029" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348896/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-348896/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348896/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6d985051-c488-50a2-aafb-4f3c91bfb279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348896/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "45841253-2a32-59e9-b236-9dd537fd51bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348896/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-348896/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348896" :question/id #uuid "fa3d60a4-4840-58c7-a2c5-661605cbc7a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-348896" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-4).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x+7=A(x-4)+B(x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(4)+7 & =A(4-4)+B(4+3) \\\\ 35 & =7B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-3)+7 & =A(-3-4)+B(-3+3) \\\\ -14 & =-7A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{5}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348896/field-1" "q-348896/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348896"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
